<blockquote>
<p>I'm not entirely sure that they'd wire her up with an ECG if she's on her deathbed and all treatment is merely palliative at this point, which is how you make it sound.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Very true. Also, if she's that far along, chances are she's either very out of it on pain medicine or she's in a lot&#8212;and I mean a <strong>lot</strong>- -of pain. I know it's a common trope (I've contributed to it myself, though there were mitigating circumstances), but the death wouldn't be all smiles and sweetness. She'd probably just be alive but unconscious for a few hours beforehand. Also, just a small thing:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The towncar sped off into the distance, bringing her someplace new.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Taking, not bringing. The Foundation is bringing her somewhere and the towncar is taking her there. Like the difference between &quot;immigrant&quot; and &quot;emigrant.&quot;</p>

